<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="48380" href="schedule/2023/spring/ME/598/48380.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2023" href="schedule/2023.xml">2023</calendarYear><term id="120231" href="schedule/2023/spring.xml">Spring 2023</term><subject id="ME" href="schedule/2023/spring/ME.xml">Mechanical Engineering</subject><course id="598" href="schedule/2023/spring/ME/598.xml">Special Topics</course></parents><sectionNumber>DM </sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Intro to Digital Materials</sectionTitle><creditHours>4 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>Meets with MSE 598 (70522) and CSE 498 (70543).  We introduce the connection of materials and data science, and specific issues regarding experimental and computational materials data. Topics include data acquisition and management, data curation, uncertainty quantification, and applying machine learning to materials data. The focus will be on current scientific literature in the emerging materials and data area.</sectionText><sectionNotes>Restricted to Graduate - Urbana-Champaign.</sectionNotes><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>CrossListOpen (Restricted)</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2023-01-17Z</startDate><endDate>2023-05-03Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LCD">Lecture-Discussion</type><start>11:00 AM</start><end>12:20 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>TR     </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>2051</roomNumber><buildingName>Sidney Lu Mech Engr Bldg</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Trinkle" firstName="D">Trinkle, D</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>